<article class="env-lemma" id="00FK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00FK">Lemma <span data-tag="00FK">10.30.5</span>.</a> Let $R \subset S$ be an injective ring map. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ hits all the minimal primes. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak p \subset R$ be a minimal prime. In this case $R_{\mathfrak p}$ has a unique prime ideal. Hence it suffices to show that $S_{\mathfrak p}$ is not zero. And this follows from the fact that localization is exact, see Proposition <a href="/tag/00CS" data-tag="00CS">10.9.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>